# mutgap3_sys_tracker_17_inner_holes: visit_unmapped_ranges holds 16 unmapped runs; a 17th inside the range is refused ("Unmapped range too complex"). Single pages 2, 4, ..., 34 are mapped (17 runs), then [35, 40), a run of its own (adjacent runs stay apart). A lazy probe of [0, 38) finds 17 holes, each before a mapped page, and no tail (the last run covers it), so the 17th is refused at the Inside case, not at the tail's check: the blocks setup cannot map the list and the exec faults with no map_memory call. The other setups map the list whole.
